  "notes": "AC 3.060-1 is the current successor of the AC 3.055-1 (no official AC 3.055-1 metric datasheet could be downloaded; Tadano Europe AC 3.055-1 page has no PDF). Datasheet also has a '10.4 m*' over-rear column (60.0 t** at 2.5 m with additional special equipment; 39.5 @3, 39.5 @3.5, 38.1 @4, 35.6 @4.5, 33.4 @5, 29.2 @6, 24.4 @7) - excluded. The 2.5 m row is empty in all 360° columns and was dropped; headline 60 t is over rear with special equipment only, max 360° value is 39.5 t @3 m. Across a row, longer booms sometimes show slightly higher values than shorter ones (e.g. 7 m: 10.4 m 24.0, 13.9 m 24.6, 17.4 m 24.7 t) - as printed. Note 1) row (capacity with horizontal boom): 10.4 m 14.4, 13.9 m 10.6, 17.4 m 8.3, 20.9 m 6.3, 24.4 m 4.8, 27.9 m 3.8, 31.4 m 2.9, 34.9 m 2.1, 38.4 m 1.5, 41.9 m 1.1 t. Notes p.42: weight of hook blocks and slings is part of the load and must be deducted. Counterweight 12.1 t = 4.7 t basic (4 pcs) + 3 additional pcs. Dimensions (p.6, mm): overall length incl. boom overhang 11668, carrier length 9326 (front bumper to rear), boom overhangs carrier front by 1941; axle spacing 3106 (front to axle 1), 2000, 2400; slewing centre 1350 ahead of axle 3; front outrigger 4200 ahead of and rear outrigger 2700 behind slewing centre; height 3610 (385/95R25) / 3660 (445/95R25); tail radius R4350 shown at counterweight (R3590 also shown). Operating weight not stated as a single figure (axle-load table p.10: 3 x <12 t = <36 t in basic config; 46 t config with 15.5 t axle loads). Max outrigger force, hook height, boom pivot position and number of boom sections not given numerically."
